From 24d0037df3fa238dd34292a706658dc70c66ca86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:26:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Block external entities and remote schemas in XML schema
 matching

XmlSchemaValidator set the JAXP properties ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD and
ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA to "all" (CWE-611, CWE-918). A schema in an
xmlSchema body matcher, and every request body validated against it,
could read local files through external entities, external DTDs,
xs:include and xs:import, and could open connections to any host. A
schema value ending in ".xsd" was read from any path (CWE-22).
StringToXmlDocumentParser, which XPath matching and JSON schema
matching of XML bodies use, also read external entities in a body.

XmlSchemaValidator now turns on secure processing, sets
ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD to "" and ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA to "file", and
sets both to "" on each Validator. A resource resolver loads
xs:include, xs:import and xs:redefine only from a regular file under
the XML schema resource root. Any other reference gets an empty
schema, and nothing is fetched from the network. External DTDs and
external entities in a schema are refused, also when they name a file
under the root. A ".xsd" value is read from the classpath, or from a
regular file under the root. The root is the working directory, or
the directory named by the new mockserver.xmlSchemaResourceRoot
setting (system property, property file or
MOCKSERVER_XML_SCHEMA_RESOURCE_ROOT). The filesystem root is never
used as the root.

StringToXmlDocumentParser now turns on secure processing and turns
off external general entities, external parameter entities and
loading of the external DTD.

A DOCTYPE with an internal subset is still accepted in schemas and in
bodies, and its internal entities still expand. Schema files under
the root keep loading.

Adds XmlSchemaValidatorExternalReferenceTest,
StringToXmlDocumentParserExternalEntityTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-pqgh-898g-975x
